      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1,700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the maximum recommended metformin dose. The limit is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A dose that high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity.\n\nThis may be a typo. Some possible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the IR maximum.\n- **1,700 mg/day in total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals**, which are common regimens.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that it's intentional and give me the clinical rationale. I'll then enter it with a note recording that confirmation."
      }
